    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0157" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1379: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-09T02:00:00-05:00">January 9, 1939—2
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 1, January 7, 3 p.m., I have sent
                    messages to other members of the Commission asking their agreement to
                    announcement of an approximate date for projected visits to Managua and to
                    Tegucigalpa. The Costa Rican member of the Commission is now in Chile and
                    possibly may visit Buenos Aires on invitation of Argentine Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
